    {
      "id": "esp_ws_client send @64",
      "target": "MID",
      "source": "static",
      "payload": 64,
      "value": 64,
      "goal": 64,
      "moved_by": "#2171 (first pin)",
      "basis": "esp_ws_client_link.cpp send: gather_into copies every span of the frame once, into the tx_ slot when another send is writing or into tx_buf_ when this one writes (1). esp_transport_write then masks the buffer in place and unmasks it after the write: two XOR passes, no copy. Payload bytes only, as the other MID rows count them; the frame's FWD envelope is copied with it. The lwIP pbuf copy is the stack's, like the kernel's on WIDE. Goal from #2136 user story 16: gather and mask in one pass, so the copy stays and the two passes go."
